1
00:00:00,238 --> 00:00:02,343
Restarting your PC can actually help.

2
00:00:02,343 --> 00:00:03,015
But if the same

3
00:00:03,015 --> 00:00:04,295
problem keeps coming back,

4
00:00:04,295 --> 00:00:05,734
restarting probably isn't fixing

5
00:00:05,734 --> 00:00:07,152
the reason it started.

6
00:00:07,152 --> 00:00:09,467
A restart can stop stuck processes,

7
00:00:09,467 --> 00:00:11,000
clear temporary activity,

8
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,019
and reload system services.

9
00:00:13,019 --> 00:00:14,733
But startup apps can launch again,

10
00:00:14,733 --> 00:00:16,686
background programs can come back,

11
00:00:16,686 --> 00:00:18,590
low storage is still low storage,

12
00:00:18,590 --> 00:00:19,743
and a problem inside one

13
00:00:19,743 --> 00:00:21,324
app may still be there.

14
00:00:21,324 --> 00:00:22,853
So if you keep restarting your PC

15
00:00:22,853 --> 00:00:24,543
just to make it feel normal again,

16
00:00:24,543 --> 00:00:25,619
it may be time to figure

17
00:00:25,619 --> 00:00:27,933
out what's actually causing the slowdown.

18
00:00:27,933 --> 00:00:29,343
Noah can check what's happening,

19
00:00:29,343 --> 00:00:30,790
explain what it finds,

20
00:00:30,790 --> 00:00:32,157
and show you what it recommends

21
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:33,952
before you approve any changes.

22
00:00:33,952 --> 00:00:35,429
Don't just restart it again.

23
00:00:35,429 --> 00:00:37,152
Check what keeps coming back.

24
00:00:37,152 --> 00:00:39,571
Free PC Check at onnoah.app.
